  "notes": "Source: Agape College of Business and Science 2023 Catalog (Revision and Print Date 03/25/2024), official PDF at acbscollege.org. Hand-transcribed 2026-09-30. QUARTER CREDITS: Agape uses a quarter-based calendar; all credit values in this file are QUARTER credits as stated in the catalog (p. 'Academic credit is given in quarter credits'). They are not semester credits. Catalog degree outlines give lecture/lab/externship hours per course; only the catalog's stated quarter-credit values are transcribed here. Quarter-by-quarter term placement is the collector's arrangement (the catalog lists courses in tables, not term sequences) and follows catalog prerequisite chains; this is disclosed, not a catalog claim. Prerequisites transcribed only from the catalog's course-description sections (asterisk legend rules applied per program); non-course prerequisites (e.g., 'all courses prior to the last quarter of enrollment') are recorded in choice_note instead of prereq. Program totals: concentration + elective 101, general education 60, specialization 20 = 181 quarter credits (catalog: 2030 total hours). The catalog's 'Elective Total 10' credits are a categorization WITHIN the listed concentration courses (listed courses sum to 101, matching the catalog's concentration total); no separate elective courses are named, so none are added. Exit requirements (not modeled as courses): Microsoft Office User Specialist certification (Word or Excel), 90 practicum + 90 internship hours, 70% overall GPA. BUS217 Practicum is the 90-hour practicum course (3 quarter credits); BUS350 is the 90-hour internship in the specialization (3 quarter credits). BT214's catalog prerequisite lists BT203, BT207, BT208, but BT208 (Data Base Management II) does not appear in the BSBA outline; the prereq is recorded verbatim from the catalog. BT208 is a catalog-listed prerequisite of BT214, offered in the AS program; recorded in external_prereqs.",
